Authorization concepts I now understand:

Authentication = "Who are you?"
Authorization = "What are you allowed to do?"
Users should only access their own data.
We should not trust a userId sent by the browser.
The server should get the authenticated user's identity using getCurrentUser().
Users can have roles such as "user" and "admin"/doctor.
Authorization checks should happen on the server.
Protected pages and protected API routes both need authorization where appropriate.

